            <ArticleTitle>Focal myositis in a patient with bilateral painful nodules.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 30-year-old African-American man presented with painful lower extremities and bilaterally symmetrical dermal nodules. Examination of a biopsy specimen of one of the nodules showed focal myositis overlying a deeper defect. Subsequent excisions produced multifocal eruptive lipomas. The histopathologic findings of focal myositis are reviewed along with this previously unreported association.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
